Source snapshot
===============

This Debian revision uses upstream commit
c8f241e960106b1b5e2c3aecdcd42a11a8a56509, based on the 1.1.4 series.
Create the original tarball from that full commit before building a source
package from the checkout.

    version=1.1.4+git20261119.c8f241e96010
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="scx-$version/" \
        c8f241e960106b1b5e2c3aecdcd42a11a8a56509 \
        | xz -T1 > "../scx_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc -d

Run sbuild for amd64 in an unstable build environment after the
Build-Depends are available. The initial package set targets Debian main.
Public archive tracking is in https://bugs.debian.org/1126281.

Build
=====

The scheduler list records each Debian package, Cargo binary, manifest
location and BPF language. Run debian/check-schedulers after updating the
upstream snapshot. The same source package builds the full list.

The build uses Rust crate packages from /usr/share/cargo/registry through
dh-rust and regenerates the root Cargo.lock offline. The clean target
restores the original root lockfile. The four independent Rust BPF
workspaces retain their upstream lockfiles and use the Cargo config
shipped by rust-src for the standard library's pinned dependencies.
Clang 22 compiles C BPF code. The bpf-linker build in the archive must
support the LLVM version used by Debian's rustc. The build fails if the
Rust BPF tooling is incomplete.

The scx scheduler manifests require libbpf-cargo and libbpf-rs 0.27.2,
libbpf-sys 1.7.1, nix 0.31 and nvml-wrapper 0.12. Debian's system libbpf
1.7.0 corresponds to libbpf-sys 1.7.1+v1.7.0. New crate packages and
bpf-linker are tracked separately. Check recursive dependencies and
crate features when making the packages available to sbuild.

Debian's dh-rust helper records source relationships for each scheduler
using that scheduler's build outputs. Set DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck to
skip the Rust binary unit tests.

Tests
=====

The autopkgtests exercise command startup with --help or --version and
verify file ownership and installation of the scx-full dependency set.

For kernel qualification, boot an amd64 VM with sched_ext and BTF
enabled. Install and exercise each scheduler with its upstream
configuration, confirm its struct_ops name and enabled state in
/sys/kernel/sched_ext, then stop it and confirm the state returns to
disabled. Mitosis and Nitosis need a cgroup hierarchy for their cells.
Confirm Nitosis on Linux 7.4 or a kernel with the required struct_ops
callback backported.

